    "chunk_size_bytes": 1823,
    "chunk_text": "Whereas I am desirous of rewarding long, efficient loyal service, and exemplary conduct of proven capacity byCommissioned Officers, Warrant Officers, Non-Commissioned Officers and Men of the Sri Lanka Army Volunteer Force.\n\nFifth Paragraph:It is ordained that the award of the Medal to such Commissioned Officer, Warrant Officers,Non-Commissioned Officers and Men of the Sri Lanka Army Volunteer Force should berecommended by the Commanding Officer of the Unit in which the period of service requisiteto qualify for the Medal is completed ; and such recommendation is certified by the Colonel ofthe Regiment and the Commandant of the Sri Lanka Army Volunteer Force and finally approvedby Commander of Sri Lanka Army as efficient and thoroughly capable Commissioned Officers,Warrant Officers, Non-Commissioned Officers or Men deserving in every way to award theMedal.\n\nSixth Paragraph:It is ordained that Commissioned Officers, Warrant Officers, Non-Commissioned Officersand Men on the Reserve of the Sri Lanka Army Volunteer Force are entitled to claim for thisMedal, if at, the time they were placed on the Reserve, they had such qualifying service requisitefor the Medal.\n\nSeventh Paragraph:It is ordained that a recipient of this medal shall not be eligible for a second conferment orconferment of clasp during his lifetime.\n\nEighth Paragraph:It is ordained that the Eighth regulation ordained previously to be null.\n\nNinthly Paragraph:It is ordained that sealed patterns of the Kariyakshama Seva Padakkama in miniature, which maybe worn on certain occasions by Commissioned Officers and Warrant Officers on whom theMedal is conferred, shall be half the size of the Kariyakshama Seva Padakkama.\n\nBY HIS EXCELLENCY MAITHRIPALA SIRISENA, PRESIDENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA\n\nSealMAITHRIPALA SIRISENA"
