    "chunk_text": "7AIV (w) jeks fldgi \u2014 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'22PART IV(A) \u2014 GAZETTE EXTRA ORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 22.11.2019\n\nAUTHORIZATION\n\nThe expenditure of the Sabaragamua Provincial Council which is estimated for the service of the period beginningon 01st January, 2019 and ending 31st December, 2019, and specified in the annual financial statement - 2019 amended byFirst Supplementary Estaimate - 2019, Rupees Thirty Four Billion Twenty Three Million Four Hundred and Six ThousandOne Hundred and Ninety Seven and Cents Twenty Four only (Rs. 34,023,406,197.24) and grant permission to disburse thesame from the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council Fund.\n\nThis permission will be valid till 31st December, 2019 or upto the date that expires 03 months from the date ofsummoning the 07th Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council or from the date re-start the functions of the Sabaragamuwa ProvincialCouncil which occurs first.\n\nDHAMMA DISSANAYAKE,Honourable Governor,Sabaragamuwa Province.\n\n16th September, 2019.\n\nAUTHORIZATION\n\nI do hereby approve to amend the advance account limits stated in the Sixth Schedule of the Second Supplementary FinancialStatement for the year 2019, by virtue of powers vested in me under Section 27 (a) of the Provincial Council Act No. 42 of1987, as the term of the 06th Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka endedon 26th September, 2017.\n\nAccordingly, I do hereby grant permission to the Chief Secretary and the Accounting Officers of the SabaragamuwaProvincial Council to bear the expenses subject to those limits.\n\nThis permission will be valid till 31st December, 2019 or upto the date that expires 03 months from the date ofsummoning the 07th Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council or from the date re-start the functions of the Sabaragamuwa ProvincialCouncil which occurs first.\n\nDHAMMA DISSANAYAKE,Honourable Governor,Sabaragamuwa Province.\n\n16th September, 2019.\n\n12 - 173"
